Subject: [PATCH 78/98] =?UTF-8?q?Find=20bar=20over=20the=20page,=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=E2=8C=98T=20history=20per=20profile?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- The find bar (⌘F) sits over the page at the top right, like Arc. It was
  placed under the URL pill, which is in the sidebar.
- Its slide runs on a timer: the WebUI window's compositor drew no frames
  for it, so the bar stayed slid out of sight and never closed on Esc.
- ⌘T in a space of another profile suggests from that profile's history:
  the command bar makes its field again when the profile changes and the
  browser binds it to the active space's profile.
- Test hooks: testKeyPress sends menu shortcuts to the test window (the
  menu targets the key window); testBubbles reads widgets from the view
  tree (the find bar's widget_delegate dangles) and can give bounds.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
